---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — WasPetInsuranceWorthIt.com"
  description="Privacy policy for WasPetInsuranceWorthIt.com. What the calculator does with your inputs, what the optional contribution button sends, and which cookies are involved."
>
  <article class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Last updated: September 2026</p>

    <h2>What the Calculator Does With Your Inputs</h2>
    <p>
      Every calculation on WasPetInsuranceWorthIt.com runs in your browser. When you enter your
      pet's species, breed, age, spending range, and incident history, those values stay on your
      device and the math is performed there. Nothing is sent to us automatically, and nothing is
      saved between visits — closing or refreshing the page clears everything you entered.
    </p>

    <h2>The Optional "Contribute My Result" Button</h2>
    <p>
      There is one exception, and it only happens if you choose it. After the calculator shows
      your result, it offers a button labelled <strong>"Contribute my result."</strong> If you
      click that button — and only then — your answers are sent to our server and stored so we can
      improve the calculator's assumptions. If you click "No thanks," or ignore the prompt
      entirely, nothing is transmitted.
    </p>
    <p>If you do contribute, this is exactly what gets stored:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Species (dog or cat) and breed</li>
      <li>Your pet's current age and the age at which you acquired them</li>
      <li>Your total vet spending range and largest single bill range (ranges, not exact amounts)</li>
      <li>The approximate percentage of that spending that was routine care</li>
      <li>Which major incident categories you selected</li>
      <li>Whether you had insurance, and whether you said you would buy it again</li>
      <li>The verdict the calculator produced and its dollar figure</li>
      <li>A timestamp and a randomly generated submission ID</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We also store a one-way SHA-256 hash of your IP address, salted with a fixed application-specific string. This is
      used to detect duplicate or automated submissions. The raw IP address is not written to the
      database, and the hash cannot be reversed back into an IP address by anyone reading the
      stored data.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not ask for and do not store your name, email address, postal address, phone number,
      or your pet's name. There is no way for us to connect a contributed result back to you.
      Aggregate statistics derived from contributed results may be published on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>No Accounts, No Mailing Lists</h2>
    <p>
      There are no user accounts on this site. There is no sign-up, no login, no newsletter, and
      no marketing list. We do not sell, rent, or share submitted data with insurance companies,
      brokers, lead generators, or any other third party.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies Set By This Site</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no first-party cookies of its own. It does not use Google Analytics or any
      other analytics or visitor-tracking service, and it does not use localStorage or similar
      browser storage to remember you between visits.
    </p>

    <h2>Google AdSense</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses Google AdSense to display advertisements. Google is a third party and may set
      its own cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this site or other websites — this
      is separate from the statement above, which covers only cookies set by us. You can opt out of
      personalized advertising by visiting{' '}
      <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Google Ads Settings
      </a>. Google's use of advertising cookies is governed by its{' '}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Privacy Policy
      </a>. We do not receive the data Google collects through those cookies, and contributed
      calculator results are never shared with Google or any advertiser.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      If the site's behaviour changes — for example, if we add a feature that collects something
      not listed above — this page will be updated to describe it before that feature ships, and
      the "last updated" date at the top will change.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this privacy policy:
      <!--email_off-->contact@waspetinsuranceworthit.com<!--/email_off-->. See the{' '}
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> for more.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
